From 4dadc46fcef53c10189e21eb33437b3db34f9100 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:22:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Graphics paging: keep unit, city and plot graphics only near
 the camera

A large game (300 cities, 2,359 units) ends with the executable's memory
allocation failure; every unit and city gets its model and every plot its
feature, route and improvement graphics, on screen or not.

CvGame::updateGraphicsPaging reads the camera's look-at plot each update and,
when it moves two plots or every 500 ms, pages graphics: inside a window around
it they are set up, outside the window and a margin they are removed. A paged-out
unit or city keeps a bare entity (created, not set up, as its constructor makes
it); a paged-out plot has no feature, route or plot-builder symbol. Visual calls
on paged-out entities are skipped (CvDLLEntity wrappers, addEntityMission, the
direct entity calls); a unit about to be shown moving or fighting, or moving
into the window, is paged in first. The active player's units and cities and
units in combat are never paged out. Graphics only: nothing is saved and the
game plays the same.

The window scales with the camera zoom (CvGameInterface.getCameraZoom, a copy
of BtS's CvGameInterface.py with that function added). Defines GRAPHICS_PAGING*
in GlobalDefinesAlt.xml; GRAPHICS_PAGING 0 restores the old behaviour.

Serves: P7, P8
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015smokgQ1KvKFbApTvkeH68
